    {
      "text": "2.1. Preliminaries",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        94.25012969970703,
        188.5855255126953,
        103.93740844726562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We start by introducing some mathematical notation. Given a vector x ∈Rn, we denote",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        111.63983154296875,
        521.9961547851562,
        123.24642944335938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "its elements as x = (x1, ..., xn). An integer coefficient vector α = (α1, ..., αn) ∈Nn defines",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        123.14917755126953,
        521.999755859375,
        137.8623046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the monomial xα = xα1",
