    },
    {
      "text": "2.2. Christoffel Functions",
      "bbox": [
        89.9998779296875,
        295.6542053222656,
        230.22547912597656,
        305.34149169921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Christoffel functions are a class of functions associated with a finite measure and a parameter",
      "bbox": [
        89.9998779296875,
        314.96319580078125,
        522.02197265625,
        324.6504821777344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "degree d ∈N. They have a strong connection to approximation theory and in this section",
      "bbox": [
        89.9998779296875,
        327.90228271484375,
        522.0587158203125,
        338.2004699707031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "we briefly summarize some results by Lasserre and Pauwels (2019). For a finite measure",
      "bbox": [
        89.9998779296875,
        342.06219482421875,
        521.9893188476562,
        351.7494812011719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "µ on Rn and an integer degree d, the Christoffel function Λµ,d(x) : Rn 7→R is defined in",
      "bbox": [
        89.9998779296875,
        351.0411682128906,
        522.01318359375,
        366.5052185058594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "terms of the moment matrix of the measure µ:",
      "bbox": [
        90.00003051757812,
        369.1600646972656,
        312.54571533203125,
        378.8473815917969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Md =",
      "bbox": [
        234.59300231933594,
        397.7690734863281,
        262.8752746582031,
        409.234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Z",
      "bbox": [
        265.90301513671875,
        390.0556335449219,
        271.9684753417969,
        397.0374755859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Rn vd(x)vd(x)⊤dµ(x).",
