    {
      "text": "In a data-driven setting, the exact measure µ is unknown. One way to obtain information",
      "bbox": [
        106.93624877929688,
        591.1651000976562,
        522.0528564453125,
        600.8524169921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "about µ is by sampling a set of points independently drawn from its distribution. For every",
      "bbox": [
        90.00022888183594,
        604.715087890625,
        522.0809326171875,
        614.4024047851562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N ∈N, when disposing of N i.i.d samples {x1, . . . , xN} from µ, we approximate µ with the",
      "bbox": [
